---
title: Why WebMCP — the same feature attempted four other ways
---
flowchart TB

  GOAL["THE REQUIREMENT<br/>An agent that can tell you WHERE the answer is<br/>in a document it is not permitted to read"]

  GOAL --> T1
  GOAL --> T2
  GOAL --> T3
  GOAL --> T4
  GOAL --> T5

  subgraph T1["Server-side MCP"]
    A1["To search the documents,<br/>the server must hold them."]
    A2["Uploading is the exact action<br/>the user is forbidden to take."]
    A3["<b>The primitive is definitionally<br/>unavailable. The server that holds<br/>the text has already read it.</b>"]
    A1 --> A2 --> A3
  end

  subgraph T2["REST API"]
    B1["No shared visual surface."]
    B2["The human cannot watch,<br/>interrupt, or approve in flow."]
    B3["<b>Per-page approval requires both<br/>parties looking at the same live page<br/>at the same moment.</b>"]
    B1 --> B2 --> B3
  end

  subgraph T3["Playwright / computer-use"]
    C1["Can drive a fresh session.<br/>Cannot JOIN the one the user is in."]
    C2["Must read the screen to know<br/>what a document says."]
    C3["<b>Confidential text passes through<br/>screenshots into the model.<br/>It defeats the boundary.</b>"]
    C1 --> C2 --> C3
  end

  subgraph T4["OS or extension agent"]
    D1["Reads the whole page<br/>or the whole filesystem."]
    D2["No structured contract for<br/>'you may know this exists and<br/>may not know what it says'."]
    D1 --> D2
  end

  subgraph T5["WebMCP"]
    E1["execute runs INSIDE the process<br/>that already holds the plaintext."]
    E2["Per-call contract with a JSON Schema<br/>and an annotation model."]
    E3["<b>Search and disclosure become two<br/>separate capabilities. This is the<br/>only place that split can exist.</b>"]
    E1 --> E2 --> E3
  end

